          "type": "text",
          "text": "Now I have very precise measurements through the true center (26, 34, 32). Let me summarize all three axial measurements:\n\n**X-scan through (y=34, z=32):**\n- Cavity enters at x\u224819 (last 1\u2192transition at x=18), fully zero at x=19\n- Cavity exits at x\u224833 (last zero at x=33, returns to 1 at x=34)\n- Center X = (19+33)/2 = **26**, radius_X = (33\u221219)/2 = **7**\n\n**Y-scan through (x=26, z=32):**\n- Cavity enters at y\u224827, exits at y\u224841\n- Center Y = (27+41)/2 = **34**, radius_Y = (41\u221227)/2 = **7**\n\n**Z-scan through (x=26, y=34):**\n- Cavity enters at z\u224825, exits at z\u224839\n- Center Z = (25+39)/2 = **32**, radius_Z = (39\u221225)/2 = **7**\n\nAll three axes agree perfectly. The cavity is a sphere of radius **7 voxels** centered at **(26, 34, 32)**.\n\n---\n\n## Results\n\n### (a) Cavity Center (voxel coordinates)\n**( x, y, z ) = ( 26, 34, 32 )**\n\nThis was determined by scanning along all three axes (X, Y, Z) through the dataset and finding the midpoint of the zero-Density (cavity) region on each axis:\n- X: cavity spans voxels 19\u201333 \u2192 center x = 26\n- Y: cavity spans voxels 27\u201341 \u2192 center y = 34\n- Z: cavity spans voxels 25\u201339 \u2192 center z = 32\n\n### (b) Cavity Radius\n**r \u2248 7 voxels**\n\nAll three orthogonal diameter measurements (X: 14 voxels, Y: 14 voxels, Z: 14 voxels) agree perfectly, confirming a spherical cavity with radius **7 voxels**. The boundary transitions are smooth (4-voxel linear ramp), so the hard-edge radius is measured at the 0-to-1 transition midpoint."
